<title>ETHIOPIA: Ethiopian Airlines says 58 dead, 52 survive crash.</title>
<headline>Ethiopian Airlines says 58 dead, 52 survive crash.</headline>
<dateline>ADDIS ABABA 1996-11-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Fifty-eight people died when a hijacked Ethiopian airliner crashed off the Comoro Islands after running out of fuel on Saturday and 52 people are known to have survived, an Ethiopian Airlines spokeswoman said on Sunday.</p>
<p>Marta Tilahun told Reuters the airline would issue a passenger list from the crashed plane later in the day. There were 175 passengers and crew on the plane, but the fate of the 65 others was not yet known.</p>
